#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31bd6c00-f798-5f52-8846-d0354e446d46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302590} {:answer/id #uuid "0f790dec-57a6-50e2-ae78-aecfd1e526bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302591} {:answer/id #uuid "3018ea92-63a7-573e-b157-ec5f717b1254" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302592} {:answer/id #uuid "1de88b45-c080-5a50-be90-5f0c5be697c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302593} {:answer/id #uuid "3569ca0f-f09b-58e7-b673-c4e366db8821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f790dec-57a6-50e2-ae78-aecfd1e526bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302591} :answer-field/id #uuid "12fc5801-5621-5551-975d-5ccdd051d75a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302589}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6b7394b-01c9-52bb-809f-2cab825b18da" :question/math-academy-id "q-115129" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/c71a52cc148f8ce4a23a2fb2005757c9d141d3caf05586d8fb5122f591dc7474.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=1$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302620 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4102dd04-292b-5aa0-be43-eaca3f7b98e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302622} {:answer/id #uuid "341d6331-272c-53ad-8d6c-f724841c85a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302623} {:answer/id #uuid "d9221f3e-391d-51e6-8eeb-3c9323e17425" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302624} {:answer/id #uuid "c0b7fde4-ca32-5996-a1e5-665eb886edf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302625} {:answer/id #uuid "062d034f-943a-5896-a335-90c666e01815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{10}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0b7fde4-ca32-5996-a1e5-665eb886edf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302625} :answer-field/id #uuid "30ca1e55-10d3-51da-aece-ec767a7ef1d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "60ed3df5-f374-5da1-8a03-7183d44bf408" :question/math-academy-id "q-69893" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/be8468d84e3820bd1e9181d31aa3a1b7d1a85c743020a69cb67fc3f601a88363.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=2$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
